body:
@Maaark I am sorry I won't have time to code this widget, I think given your level of understanding of the library you could give a try at doing it.

You could start with a simple:

```js
var widget = {
  init: function() {
    // define the options you need
  },
  render: function() {
    // empty the select and update the options accordingly
  }
}
```

There's one thing though that will not be feasible I believe is that you will not be able to hide some options if they are not matching any record, because we do not compute that data in Algolia REST API.
